Z||000000||fierospeeder||01-27-2000||01:14 AM||||I was looking through my thick chiltons manual for cars ranging in years of 80 to 87.<P>The highest hp and torque i found was for this buick engine i was wondering if i can do the swap, eventhough everyone says the 3.8 is the hardest.<BR>Im not sure what kind of car, i think its the regal.<P>Vin code 7   6-231 engine type   fuel delivery is SFI   hp 235@4400 torque 330@2800<BR>this is the readings off the wheels.<BR>I think the engine is a turbo.  8:1 compression.  <P>That would be good hp for me swapping from a 100hp four cylinder.  My questions, what mods do i have to do, i can do fuel and coolant lines on my own and wiring.  I just need to know about engine mounts.  Will my automatic trans take that much torque?<BR>||||reg||5
